{"name":"High Risk Red","hex":"#c71f2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:\n Very elevated; extending or being far above a base; tall; lofty.","Very elevated; extending or being far above a base; tall; lofty."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In or to an elevated position.","In or at a great value."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high"},{"term":"risk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The probability of a negative outcome to a decision or event.","The magnitude of possible loss consequent to a decision or event."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To incur risk of (an unwanted or negative outcome).","To incur risk of harming or jeopardizing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Risk","blocks":[{"text":"Risk is the possibility of something bad happening, comprising a level of uncertainty about the effects and implications of an activity, particularly negative and undesirable consequences."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/3_Alarm_Building_Fire.jpg/330px-3_Alarm_Building_Fire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Risk","wikidata":"Q104493"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible